# Woo Goes Further (Longshot & DavyB, ASL 550, v2.3): full win (state Finished, no clock needed). Older sibling of Woo Rebooted but a DIFFERENT layout: the single endgame is `pull handle` in the BARDIS with the mercury-filled fluid link in the control console AND a toilet roll in the holder (the Hambo party invitation is optional).
# Chain: Kojak's final speech hands over the gold sovereign, which is the only thing the Shop's toilet roll accepts; the sovereign needs the murder solved first, so most of the route is the Cluedo case (cottage key, Camera Shop photo -> Bolt egg, onion, McIntosh canister + ticket, bread, library book swap, Paxo recipe, Bilbo ticket + platform shoes, hell herbs, Little Chef stuffing, Tom's sunglasses, Custard clues -> accuse Mrs Seadock with notebook choice `5`).
# Footguns handled: money order (each sale feeds the next); never walk into the Police Station / Study carrying the candlestick (Kojak arrests you) and drop it before the accusation; the welcome mat in inventory gets you thrown out of the Tavern; Killer Chickens south of the Meadow are fatal without the stuffing; tweezers block `up` the beanstalk; `unlock shutters` (not `use key on`); `take white card` for the psychic paper; Number 66 vs Patrick McGoogle needs `give passport to number 66` first; the thesaurus is read twice for the blanket; the cellar rat leads to the fishing line -> magnet chain; Study drawer is emptied before Sharples; the sneeze auto-fires; Mad Donna depends on the seeded RNG.
# Teleporter: every `port X` is issued twice (the second prints "You Are Already There") so a missed stop does not desync the script; stops are only added once visited (Bilbo's House on foot first); `port` fails in the Hell garden and the Manor Study (Weak Signal) and underground (caves). After the accusation DEFCON is 1 and only `port x` works until Seadock is arrested in the bunker; `push small black button` resets it.
# Endgame: the lit candlestick is fetched back from Custard's office (the caves are dark without it); laughing gas on the Incredible Sulk at the Giant Stalagmite moves him to the Mountain Trail where `ask sulk about boulder axe` frees the axe; the giant on Green Hill is satisfied by white tulips + red roses + huge tweezers + hairdressing voucher (smelling salts on the beer-stunned Vidal Monsoon); the reporters only leave after the beanstalk is chopped at Jack's Garden and the newspaper updates while you stand on Green Hill (`tell reporters about doctor black`); mercury is taken at Mercury Swamp (jumpsuit + gas mask worn); `pull handle` once reveals the holder, then take the cardboard tube out before `put toilet roll in holder`.
